@startuml Builder_AlbumReportBuilder
' If any modifications are done to the classes participating in this pattern,
' this diagram must be updated accordingly.

title Builder Pattern — AlbumReportBuilder

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FEFECE
  BorderColor #A80036
}

note as N1
  <b>BUILDER (Creational)</b>
  IAlbumReportBuilder defines the construction steps.
  AlbumReportBuilder accumulates file results in a
  thread-safe manner using the C# 13 .lock type,
  then assembles the final AlbumReport product.
  AlbumUploadState acts as the Director.
end note

interface IAlbumReportBuilder << Builder >> {
  + AddSuccess(fileName : string) : IAlbumReportBuilder
  + AddFailure(fileName : string, reason : string) : IAlbumReportBuilder
  + Build() : AlbumReport
}

class AlbumReportBuilder << ConcreteBuilder >> {
  - _lock : Lock
  - _accepted : List<string>
  - _rejected : List<(string, string)>
  - telegramId : long
  + AddSuccess(fileName : string) : IAlbumReportBuilder
  + AddFailure(fileName : string, reason : string) : IAlbumReportBuilder
  + Build() : AlbumReport
}

class AlbumReport << Product >> {
  + TelegramId : long
  + GeneratedAt : DateTime
  + Accepted : IReadOnlyList<string>
  + Rejected : IReadOnlyList<(string, string)>
  + ToMarkdown() : string
}

class AlbumUploadState << Director >> {
  + HandleAlbumDoneCommandAsync(ctx, ct) : Task<string>
}

note right of AlbumReportBuilder
  Uses C# 13 `Lock` (.lock keyword)
  instead of object for thread-safe
  step accumulation.
end note

IAlbumReportBuilder <|.. AlbumReportBuilder
AlbumReportBuilder ..> AlbumReport : <<builds>>
AlbumUploadState ..> AlbumReportBuilder : <<uses>>
AlbumUploadState ..> IAlbumReportBuilder : <<directs>>

@enduml
